      "side": 1,
      "message": "This currently does not benefit from retrying the loose ref locks as lockLooseRefs() does, so it could fail more easily. Now, it would be easy to move the call to lockLoosRefs() before this. If we did, we would get the benefit of early return when there\u0027s nothing to lock, retry more, and more importantly we could continue to hold the loose ref locks for both repacks (if we pass them in as heldlocks to both repacks), decreasing the chance of being slowed down or even failing the transaction if the locks are grabbed by another thread.",
